/Title (Figure 1 shows how these roles fit into a progression. The path begins with a Foundation stage \(basic programming, database concepts, UI/UX fundamentals, and workflow and automation\), moves to the Low-Code Developer stage \(application development, forms and reports, and business workflows\), and then to Specialized Roles \(Automation Developer, Integration Developer and Business Application Developer\). Advanced Roles \(Low-Code Consultant, Solution Developer and Platform Specialist\) follow, and the path leads to Leadership roles \(Solution Architect, Technical Lead and Enterprise Application Architect\). The strip at the bottom of the figure lists the core skills that support all of these stages.)
